{
  "_comment": [
    "Cross-language canonical-byte vectors for the v5 signed pairing invite:",
    "a host reached THROUGH A RELAY. The Rust host signs; the Kotlin client",
    "verifies. If the two canonical encodings diverge by one character,",
    "EVERY signature fails to verify - and it fails silently, on a phone,",
    "with both sides compiling and both sides' own tests green. This file is",
    "what catches that in CI instead.",
    "",
    "v5 IS NOT A SUCCESSOR TO v4. Both are current: the number names the",
    "ROUTE. A bound host emits v4 with `addr` and `port`; a host that",
    "dialled out to a relay emits v5 with `relay_addr`, `relay_port` and the",
    "`session` the relay issued, and NO host address at all, because there",
    "is none.",
    "",
    "Both directions are recorded on purpose. `rust_generated` is verified by",
    "Kotlin; `kotlin_generated` is verified by Rust. One side alone would",
    "only prove that side is self-consistent.",
    "",
    "Regenerate deliberately, never by hand:",
    "  cargo run -p pairing --example generate_relay_vector",
    "  (cd apk && ./gradlew :app:testDebugUnitTest --tests '*InviteV5Test*' --rerun-tasks)",
    "then read KOTLIN_VECTOR lines out of the test XML system-out.",
    "",
    "Field order in canonical_utf8 is LOAD-BEARING and is not alphabetical.",
    "`session` sits with `relay_addr` and `relay_port` because the three",
    "together are 'where to connect and what to ask for'."
  ],
